ds of thadius's tormentor  are representative of his abusive  temperament  when thadius boasting newfound power  shows up to a board of directors meeting  to confront his father  sid snarls don't make me throw you out  of here  that you don't need to make a scene  after this thaad throws sid out the  window instead  in birds of prey huntress racks up a  significant body count  among her kills is victor zaz a serial  killer and  employee of roman cyanus zaz is paranoid  and neurotic working with dinah lance  aka black canary at roman's instruction  but never fully trusting her shortly  before he dies he lets loose on her  after discovering that local thief  cassandra kane has swallowed the coveted  bertinelli diamond  saying that he knew dinah couldn't be  trusted and that roman can only trust  him  dinah tells him he's just being paranoid  yeah mm-hmm prove it to me  rip open her little tummy yeah that's  not gonna happen  now that's the last thing he says before  huntress  shoots him and dinah and harley finish  the job girls gotta stick together  black mask serves as something of a  second joker to harley quinn his  patterns of intimidation and abuse to  her and the women around her nearly  break her  after engaging in a tense exchange with  him as he lurks in the shadows  during which harley realizes that mr  jay's figures are not her protectors but  her tormentors she tries and fails to  shoot black mask hitting a decoy instead  he taunts her insinuating that she  doesn't stand a chance to defeat him but  harley isn't the same harley any longer  she's undergone major changes in the way  she thinks about herself and what she  deserves  harley even tells cassandra that she  made her want to be a less terrible  person  pretty much the opposite of the impacts  the joker or black mask have ever had on  her  roman's reply not very iconic for final  words but a fitting summation of the  condescension harley faces  his final dismissal means nothing to the  two young women however  especially since cassandra has planted a  bomb on him harley kicks the villain off  the bridge  as the grenade detonates watchmen begins  with rorschach discovering a  terrible truth and he eventually dies  doing the same thing  he tries to warn his fellow vigilantes  in the interim but they don't really  take him seriously  still his quest to alert them displays  his doggedness  this is in contrast to those around him  when an old compatriot ponders what  happened to the good old days of working  together  rorschach dismisses him by calling him a  quitter something rorschach  could never do his sense of duty an  obsessive personality  keep him on the streets but they also  alienate him from everyone he's ever  called an ally or  even a friend his final surrender comes  as a sacrifice in service of truth  and his devotion to it after he watches  ozymandias traumatize the world  he realizes the enormity of what's  placed on him  he has information that could bring the  world crumbling down  and just as in the beginning he can't  commit to keeping it quiet  and so he implores dr manhattan to kill  him what are you  waiting for  [Music]  he shouts one more time and dr manhattan  obliges  leaving nothing but a bloody patch in  the snow  though the live-action batman films  sustained plenty of casualties on the  villains side  most of them are minor characters after  all batman's no kill rule is central to  his identity and has deep roots in his  violent origins the joker as a result  rarely dies in any batman related media  batman has reflected before on how he  can't ever kill the joker because he  wants to so badly  he knows that if he gave into that  impulse he might not be able to pull  back  the death of jack nicholson's joker in  1989's batman  is appropriately enough preceded by  these words  sometimes  it's a demise of his own design all  batman does is tether him to a gargoyle  and the joker's attempted escape  leads to his fatal fall batman keeps t