s  watched his name  burn for eight years to keep gotham  standing  but bats will weather the fires of the  city's hatred forever  if it means that gotham is safe from the  flames this  shrinks is one that bane can never match  and never completely kill  rosal ghoul's death in batman begins  reflects batman's ongoing  internal struggle between good and evil  the villain was once batman's savior and  mentor  without him there would be no batman at  all  and yet he's corrupt and batman has to  make his peace with that  if he can the two adversaries brawl on a  runaway train transporting a microwave  emitter that will be used against gotham  roz holds the upper hand on his foe but  eventually batman takes control  raz still taunts our hero when it looks  like batman is going to kill him  and asks do you finally learn to do what  is necessary  batman replies that he wouldn't take  raw's life but he also  doesn't have to save him in his last  moments roz realizes that batman is  indeed equipped to win  against injustice injustice like him  batman is simply doing what roz taught  him he's devoting himself to an ideal  batman's commitment to compassion is  alien to  the league of shadows is a bit more  let's just say  not compassionate when it comes to well  everything  this devotion makes bruce more than an  ordinary man in a cape  as ross claims at the start of their  throwdown it makes him legendary  though the main villains in batman vs  superman dawn of justice weren't human  there were certainly a couple of earthly  adversaries who made things  difficult for the good guys for part of  the film two of the most  vicious of these african terrorist  general amaza and russian mercenary  anatoly kenyazev were working together  and their last words have a similar ring  to them  though he didn't have as big of a role  in this film kenyasev is the alter ego  of a dc comics super villain known as kg  beast fans are hoping that somehow or  other the character will get another  